https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct

Training integrations use LLaMA-Factory, VERL, DeepSpeed, Transformers, and
vLLM. ChartAdept's VERL extensions in chartadept/rl/ adapt the upstream
actor, rollout, and reward interfaces; these dependencies are installed
separately and are not vendored here.
https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory
https://github.com/volcengine/verl
https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed
https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm

Evaluation uses the ChartVerse-style CompassVerifier rubric. The helper
scripts/fetch_compass_rubric.py retrieves the prompt constants from the
upstream evaluation implementation; that third-party prompt is not
relicensed or bundled as original ChartAdept code.
https://github.com/starriver030515/ChartVerse/blob/main/eval/verify.py

The three qualitative examples describe held-out CharXiv-RQ trajectories.
The three case illustrations and their source chart/crop assets in docs/assets/,
along with the associated records in examples/qualitative/,
are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0, following the CharXiv dataset license.
Attribution, original source-paper links, and the changes made for display
are documented in docs/assets/README.md. Full benchmarks are not bundled.
https://github.com/princeton-nlp/CharXiv
https://huggingface.co/datasets/princeton-nlp/CharXiv
